 2. Targeting a turnaround 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Target CEO Michael Fiddelke said 95% of the retailer's back-to-school items are priced at or below last year's prices. Photo: Michael M. Santiago/Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Target shares jumped after the retailer this morning reported a sharp uptick in grocery sales and online delivery.

 🌤️ The big picture: Signs of a turnaround are accelerating under its new CEO. 📊 By the numbers: Target posted a comparable store sales increase of 2.7% in the period ended Aug. 1, beating S&amp;P Capital IQ expectations of 2.5%.

 Comparable digital sales grew 8.7% as its same-day delivery service soared 25%. The company also raised its revenue and earnings outlook for the full year. Zoom in: Michael Fiddelke, who took over the top job in February, credited improvements in the company's food and home furnishings sections and benefits from its brand partnerships.

 🗣️ What they're saying: "The early stages of the merchandise-led turnaround appear to be working," D.A. Davidson analyst Michael Baker wrote today in a research note.

