 4. Linked in 😘 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Allie Carl/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 LinkedIn is a professional networking site that, it turns out, can also lead to something more.

 State of play: Members are increasingly using the service to find romantic partners, WSJ reports .

 One dating coach told WSJ that she encourages clients to use LinkedIn to reach out to romantic interests — but that the first message should be subtle. Friction point: LinkedIn says users are looking for love in all the wrong places — using it to find dates is against the rules.

 "Our focus is on making sure that people are safe from unwanted romantic advances," a LinkedIn spokesperson told WSJ. 💭 Nathan's thought bubble: With significant dating app fatigue , it's no wonder that people are looking for alternative ways to find a spark.

 
 
